// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/trinet/tern_tc_reopen_ax7203.t27 -- pre-registration: the same 8-token igla-coder generation
; on the AX7203 node, with retransmits, and the serial port closed and opened again when a resync
; meets a silent line
; The one source for this run. conformance/tern_tc_reopen_from_spec.mjs compiles this file with the
; t27 compiler (wasm), evaluates every test block below, checks the pinned files, reads back the
; constants it repeats from the generation and retransmit specs' generated params, and writes
; conformance/tern_tc_reopen_params.py, which the runner conformance/tern_tc_generate_reopen_ax7203.py
; reads. `--check` fails on drift. Written 2026-09-27 before any run of it. ASCII, English.

; WHY. The pre-registered retransmit run (specs/trinet/tern_tc_retransmit_ax7203.t27) failed in call
; 145 of 192: a short read collected 11 bytes, the next two resyncs collected 0 bytes each, and job
; 16873 reached its attempts ceiling of 3. Calls 1 to 144 had no transport event. Four minutes later
; a freshly opened port gave 3840/3840 with the key still held, so the FPGA had not been
; reconfigured. That run stays FAIL in conformance/TERN_TC_RETRANSMIT.md. This is a new claim with its
; own record, conformance/TERN_TC_REOPEN.md, not a second attempt at the old one.

; WHAT CHANGES. Only the link. conformance/tern_tc_reopen.py wraps the port under the retransmit
; protocol, which is imported unchanged and pinned by sha256. The protocol writes FLUSH_BYTES zero
; bytes once per resync and nowhere else. When the link sees that flush after zero answer bytes since
; the previous flush, the line was silent through a whole resync; the link then closes the port, waits
; REOPEN_WAIT_S doubled for each earlier reopen in the run, opens it again with the harness's own
; SerialLink (which clears the input buffer), and only then passes the flush on. An ordinary hole
; never triggers it: the answers around a hole are bytes.
; MAX_ATTEMPTS rises from 3 to 4. In the retransmit run a stalled job spent its second nonce on the
; dead port, so with the reopen before the third there would be no spare. Every other ceiling is the
; retransmit run's. Jobs, activations, model, harness, node RTL and bitstream are the generation
; run's, pinned below.

; WHAT IS NEVER RETRIED (the run stops). Everything the retransmit spec lists, with MAX_ATTEMPTS
; nonces per job; and a reopen past MAX_REOPENS.

; PREDICTION (board). Token ids == CPU_INT_IDS of the generation spec; every one of JOBS_EXPECTED
; jobs credited by exactly one answer whose tag verifies under the node key; every row bit-exact;
; retransmits <= MAX_RETRANSMITS; resyncs <= MAX_RESYNCS; reopens <= MAX_REOPENS; one node id
; throughout; elapsed <= LIMIT_S. The runner prints `receipts verified (tag) : N/N` only then, and the
; retransmit, resync and reopen counts next to it, whatever they are.
; The hypothesis is tested only if a stop like the retransmit run's happens. If the run passes with 0
; reopens, it says generation finished; it does not say a reopen clears a stop. If a reopen happens
; and the run passes, the reopen cleared that stop. If it fails with ReopenExhausted or a job past its
; attempts after a reopen, a reopen does not clear it, at these waits.
; PREDICTION (rehearsal, no board). The whole run through the reference cell behind the RTL's frame
; parser, with the retransmit spec's five losses and the two stalls below, ends REHEARSAL OK with the
; same ids and counts, at least one retransmit per scheduled loss, and exactly REHEARSAL_STALLS
; reopens: one per stall, none for the ordinary losses.
; WHAT IT DOES NOT SAY. It does not find which side stalls (node TX, CP2102N, hub or host driver).
; It does not say the UART is lossless. It is not speed and not text. One attempt; a second only if
; the first fails before its first job, and then both are recorded.

module trinet_tern_tc_reopen_ax7203;

pub const KIND : str = "board-run-preregistration";
pub const ID : str = "trinet/tern_tc_reopen_ax7203";
pub const GENERATED : [1]str = ["conformance/tern_tc_reopen_params.py"];
pub const RUNNER : str = "conformance/tern_tc_generate_reopen_ax7203.py";
pub const RECORD_DOC : str = "conformance/TERN_TC_REOPEN.md";
pub const LOG_NAME : str = "gen_tokens_8_reopen";

; --- Code and data of record: imported or read, never edited --------------------------------
pub const GENERATE_SPEC_FILE : str = "specs/trinet/tern_tc_generate_ax7203.t27";
